{"onward":{"id":"fa084b0e-21b7-4d48-8a70-2e34c9d4718b","word":"onward","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"In a forward direction","word":"para diante"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"In a forward direction","word":"a partir de agora"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"In a forward direction","word":"avante"}],"pos":"adv","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"[…] yonder cloud\nThat rises upward always higher,\n⁠And onward drags a labouring breast,\n⁠And topples round the dreary west,\nA looming bastion fringed with fire.","ref":"1850, [Alfred, Lord Tennyson], “Canto XV”, in In Memoriam, London: Edward Moxon, […], →OCLC, page 24:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[55,61]],"id":"905db26b-fd06-40f2-a3e7-a3ad81ee8524"},{"text":"Onward Christian soldiers, marching as to war...","ref":"1871, “Onward, Christian Soldiers”, Sabine Baring-Gould (lyrics):","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[0,6]],"id":"5a09cc6a-bce6-45d6-9036-cfc2737cc143"}],"links":[["direction","direction"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations"],"glosses":["In a forward direction."],"tags":["not-comparable"],"id":"a6f71184-c58d-4ec4-969d-9c994f9b47c6"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[{"word":"onwards"},{"word":"forth"}]}}
